  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Reading the arrows",
      "items": [
        "Every arrow means \"imports\": the tail depends on the head",
        "A tier may import its own and every tier to its right, never to its left",
        "internal/layout reads the tier from the import path and fails the build on an upward edge"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "What the split buys",
      "items": [
        "server/ is a second Go module, so it can depend on the library and never the reverse",
        "Importing mdmprotocol/mdm brings nine dependencies and no database driver",
        "pki/pushcert imports nothing, so storage can validate a certificate without depending on push"
      ]
    }
  ]
